# Authoring fixture: scripted user conversations for the remember-guidance comparison (probe_cli.authoring).
# One JSON object per line: id, case, today (ISO date rendered into the agent instructions), turns (user turns, played in order), targets.
# targets[].turn is a 0-based index into turns. Every target turn ends with an explicit save request, so every arm writes.
# User turns never depend on the assistant reply.
# must_mention: names a self-contained statement contains: the resolved referent, and for elliptical-referent and conversation-dependency also the situation. Scored as case-insensitive substring hits against the remember contents of that turn only; a diagnostic, never the verdict.
# reader_checks: yes/no questions a person answers per target, and the verdict: referent resolved, relative date resolved, situation named, source and qualification kept, no inference written as something the user said, corrected statement stands alone. A calendar date the user gave without a year passes as said; the date check covers relative expressions only.
# Domains are independent of the other probe fixtures, the packaged prompts, the server text and the ops client prompt.
{"id": "elliptical-referent", "case": "elliptical-referent", "today": "2026-06-02", "turns": ["I'm organising the Larkspur Road residents' gala on July 11, and I've just booked a bouncy castle from a company called Hopscotch Hire.", "About 40 households have said they're coming.", "It needs a power socket within 30 metres of wherever it's set up. Please save that."], "targets": [{"turn": 2, "must_mention": ["bouncy castle", "Larkspur"], "reader_checks": ["Does the memory attach the power requirement to the bouncy castle from Hopscotch Hire rather than an unnamed 'it'?", "Does it name the Larkspur Road residents' gala on July 11 as the situation?", "Is the requirement kept as stated (a socket within 30 metres), with nothing added?", "Is every relative time expression the memory carries written as an unambiguous date or period?"]}]}
{"id": "conversation-dependency", "case": "conversation-dependency", "today": "2026-01-19", "turns": ["I've decided to sit the Level 3 sommelier certificate this October.", "My boss has promised me the head of wine job if I pass, which is the whole reason I'm doing it.", "Blind tasting is my weak spot, so I've been looking for a course that drills it.", "Corvina Academy's course is £1,400 and only runs on Tuesday nights. Please save that."], "targets": [{"turn": 3, "must_mention": ["Corvina", "sommelier"], "reader_checks": ["Does the memory say the Corvina Academy course is blind-tasting preparation for the Level 3 sommelier certificate?", "Does it keep the price (£1,400) and the Tuesday-nights-only schedule as stated?", "Does it avoid saying the user has enrolled or decided to take the course?", "Is every relative time expression the memory carries written as an unambiguous date or period (here 'this October' is October 2026)?"]}]}
{"id": "reported-uncertain", "case": "reported-uncertain", "today": "2026-09-14", "turns": ["One of our two beehives has had almost no activity at the entrance this week.", "A bee inspector, Halvard Lunde, came out this morning to look at it.", "Halvard thinks the colony has probably lost its queen, and we might merge it with the other hive next month. Save that for me."], "targets": [{"turn": 2, "must_mention": ["Halvard", "hive"], "reader_checks": ["Is the lost queen attributed to Halvard Lunde as his probable view rather than stated as fact?", "Is merging next month kept as a possibility, not a decision?", "Does the memory name the inactive beehive, one of the user's two hives?", "Is every relative time expression the memory carries written as an unambiguous date or period (here 'next month' is October 2026)?"]}]}
{"id": "implied-consequence", "case": "implied-consequence", "today": "2026-03-02", "turns": ["My cousin Marisol is coming over from Lisbon to stay with us for a week, arriving March 20.", "It's her first time in this country, so she's made a long list of things she wants to see.", "Also, I've been called for jury service from March 23 to March 27. Save that one."], "targets": [{"turn": 2, "must_mention": ["jury"], "reader_checks": ["Does the memory keep jury service from March 23 to March 27 as the user said?", "Is any link to Marisol's visit from March 20 either absent or explicitly marked as inferred, never attributed to the user?", "Does the memory avoid stating as fact a consequence the user never said, such as having less time to host Marisol?", "Is every relative time expression the memory carries written as an unambiguous date or period?"]}]}
{"id": "correction", "case": "correction", "today": "2026-10-05", "turns": ["I'm exhibiting my model railway layout at the Quillmere Model Railway Exhibition on October 24 at the Corn Exchange. Please remember that.", "I still need to finish the signal box, so I'd better get gluing.", "Correction: the exhibition is the 27th, not the 24th. Save that instead."], "targets": [{"turn": 0, "must_mention": ["Quillmere", "railway"], "reader_checks": ["Does the memory record the user exhibiting their model railway layout at the Quillmere Model Railway Exhibition on October 24 at the Corn Exchange?", "Is every relative time expression the memory carries written as an unambiguous date or period?"]}, {"turn": 2, "must_mention": ["Quillmere", "railway"], "reader_checks": ["Does the corrected memory stand alone: the Quillmere Model Railway Exhibition at the Corn Exchange on October 27, readable without the earlier memory?", "Is October 24 no longer presented as the current date, whether corrected in the text, superseded or forgotten?", "Is every relative time expression the memory carries written as an unambiguous date or period?"]}]}
